'' A '#cmdline' IN ANY BUT THE FIRST SOURCE FILE IS A WARNING, not a restart. See
'' the sources' headers: this is fbc's rule, measured, and it matters because the
'' alternative is a file whose options are honoured or ignored depending on the
'' order its caller happened to name it in, with nothing said either way.
''
'' The build still succeeds: the directive is dropped, not fatal.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/driver/src/cmdline-first.bas tests/driver/src/cmdline-second.bas -o tests/driver/cmdlinelater.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: TKO0334
'' EXPECT-OUT: #cmdline is ignored outside the first source file
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/driver/cmdlinelater.exe
